{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added per-feed `fetch_timeout` (integer seconds, 0 = use global timeout).\n\n- New migration adds `feeds.fetch_timeout int not null default 0`; the column is read and written by feed create, update and the feed query.\n- `fetch_timeout` appears in the API feed object and is accepted by `PUT /v1/feeds/{feedID}`; negative values are rejected with an untranslated English error message (no locale key was added).\n- `Feed.HTTPClientTimeout()` returns the per-feed value when > 0, otherwise the global timeout. It is used for feed refresh, entry scraping (crawler and manual fetch of original content) and icon fetching.\n- Go client models got the field too.\n\nNot done: no web UI form field, no OPML import/export, and it is not accepted on feed creation \u2014 only on update. Subscription discovery and the reading-time/YouTube/Bilibili helpers still use the global timeout.\n\nExisting unit and integration tests pass; no tests were added for the new behaviour.", "t": 1794463060.896}
